l": "RETRACTED on the same ground and by the same construction. the_tail.top20_share_of_total_excess is UNAFFECTED and reproduces exactly, because its numerator and denominator are both width-weighted excess sums over the same domain.", "4_WHAT_SURVIVES_AND_IS_STRENGTHENED": "same_domain.median_per_cell_ratio 1.000323195109291 is weighting-independent and stands. This receipt's VERDICT -- that the offset is a concentrated tail and not a bias -- is CORRECT and is better supported than this receipt made it: dropping the 63 moves the width-weighted total ratio to 0.99471. Do not read this correction as overturning the receipt's conclusion.", "5_THE_READING_FIELD_IS_SUPERSEDED_ON_ONE_POINT": "This receipt's READING routes the open question to the acceptance-supported vs model-dependent tiering item. Measured: that convention's criterion is acceptance (a_b<0.02) and it selects ZERO of the 63, whose median a_b is 0.859 -- the highest on the grid. The 63 are also all 63 cells MINERvA itself published (Phys. Rev. D 104 (2021) 092007 data release). So the tiering item does not dispose of them, and what IS open is that the nominal lies above all 50 replicas in 44 of the 63 -- filed as OI-126, and NOT a reporting-tier question.", "6_stale_pointer": "This receipt's 'OPEN_ITEMS:430-438' is stale (BEN-228): docs/OPEN_ITEMS.md is 140 lines and the item is in docs/OPEN_ITEMS-ARCHIVE-2026-08.md. Four other artifacts carry the same stale pointer."}}
